<section style="padding:3rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Why Partner with SDF Clothing?</h2><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">We source GOTS-certified organic cotton directly and process it through our own facility, maintaining chain-of-custody documentation from fiber to finished garment rather than relying on a trading company's paperwork. That direct control is what lets us guarantee the organic claim on your label holds up under audit. GOTS, OEKO-TEX Standard 100, BSCI, WRAP, and ISO 9001 certification applies across the facility.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">GOTS certification covers ecological and social criteria across the entire supply chain, from how the cotton is grown through dyeing, finishing, and labeling — a stricter standard than OEKO-TEX, which only tests the finished product. Minimum order starts at 300 pieces per style, with fabric sourcing, sampling, bulk manufacturing, quality inspection, and export documentation handled in-house.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Two trade facts matter for organic cotton sourced here: Bangladesh keeps EU duty-free access under Everything But Arms until 2029 regardless of this November's LDC graduation, and a 20% cap on US tariffs from late 2025 limits exposure versus Chinese-sourced organic cotton under Section 301. Both help offset the certified-organic premium over conventional fiber.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem">Ready to start? <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Request a sample</a> or <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">contact our team</a> for a detailed FOB quote within 48 hours.</p></div></section>
